## Description

When a `long.MinValue` constant ends up as a typed literal in the generated SQL, the PostgreSQL provider renders
it as `-9223372036854775808::BigInt`. In PostgreSQL the `::` cast binds tighter than the unary minus, so the
server evaluates `-(9223372036854775808::bigint)`. `9223372036854775808` is one above the bigint range, and the
query fails:

```
