### Description

A single-value association declared with `QueryExpressionMethod` and `CanBeNull = true`, whose expression is a `Take(1)` subquery joined to another table, drops rows when eager-loaded with `ThenLoad`. 6.x moves the `join` out of the `OUTER APPLY`, so child rows with no match disappear from the loaded collection. 5.4.1.9 keeps the join inside the `OUTER APPLY` and returns them with a null association.

SQL from 5.4.1.9:

```sql
FROM [Sys] [lw_Sys]
    INNER JOIN [Stage] [x] ON [x].[SystemId] = [lw_Sys].[Id]
    OUTER APPLY (
        SELECT [o].[Id], [o].[Name]
        FROM (SELECT TOP (@take) [x_1].[OrganisationId] FROM [OrgSys] [x_1] WHERE [x_1].[Id] = [x].[OrgSysId]) [a]
            INNER JOIN [Org] [o] ON [a].[OrganisationId] = [o].[Id]
    ) [a_Organisation]
```

SQL from 6.5.0 and 6.5.1:

```sql
FROM [Sys] [m_1]
    INNER JOIN [Stage] [d] ON [d].[SystemId] = [m_1].[Id]
    OUTER APPLY (SELECT TOP (1) [x].[OrganisationId] FROM [OrgSys] [x] WHERE [x].[Id] = [d].[OrgSysId]) [a_Organisation]
    INNER JOIN [Org] [o] ON [a_Organisation].[OrganisationId] = [o].[Id]
```

### Workaround in place

Workaround that worked for us: write the association as an `EXISTS` instead of `Take(1)` + `join`, so there's no join for 6.x to move out of the `OUTER APPLY`.

Before (drops stages with no match on 6.x):

```cs
public static Expression<Func<Stage, IDataContext, IQueryable<Org>>> GetOrg() =>
    (s, db) => from a in db.GetTable<OrgSys>().Where(x => x.Id == s.OrgSysId).Take(1)
               join o in db.GetTable<Org>() on a.OrganisationId equals o.Id
               select o;
```

After (keeps both stages on 5.4.1.9, 6.5.0 and 6.5.1):

```cs
public static Expression<Func<Stage, IDataContext, IQueryable<Org>>> GetOrg() =>
    (s, db) => db.GetTable<Org>()
        .Where(o => db.GetTable<OrgSys>().Any(a => a.Id == s.OrgSysId && a.OrganisationId == o.Id));
```

`OrgSys.Id` is the primary key, so dropping `Take(1)` doesn't change the result.

